              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The link you provided, **`mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`**, is a legacy (older) URL for the **Georgia Department of Revenue's (DOR) Motor Vehicle Division (MVD)**. \n\nIn recent years, Georgia consolidated and modernized its vehicle services under the **Georgia DRIVES** and **MyMVD** platforms. If you are looking to renew your vehicle registration (\"tags\"), check title status, or perform other motor vehicle tasks, you should use the updated official portals.\n\n### \ud83c\udf10 Official Current Portals\n* **Georgia DRIVES e-Services Portal:** **[eservices.drives.ga.gov](https://eservices.drives.ga.gov/)**\n  * This is the official secure portal for handling vehicle services online.\n* **Georgia DOR Motor Vehicles Page:** **[dor.georgia.gov/motor-vehicles](https://dor.georgia.gov/motor-vehicles)**\n  * This page has helpful forms, guides, and policies concerning license plates, titles, and insurance requirements.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\ude97 Common Tasks You Can Do Online\nThrough the official **Georgia DRIVES** portal, you can:\n* **Renew Vehicle Tags/Registration:** You will need your license plate number or VIN, along with either your Driver\u2019s License number or the Letter ID printed on your physical renewal notice.\n* **Estimate TAVT (Title Ad Valorem Tax):** Estimate the one-time title tax for newly purchased vehicles or vehicles being brought into the state by new residents.\n* **Pre-apply for Title & Registration:** Fill out the paperwork online to speed up your trip to a physical county tag office.\n* **Cancel Registration:** If you sell a vehicle or take it off the road, you can voluntarily cancel your registration online. *(Make sure to do this before cancelling your auto insurance to avoid state fines!)*\n* **MyMVD Accounts:** Georgia offers a \"MyMVD\" portal where you can view all registered vehicles tied to your driver's license in one place and easily order replacements.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Security Warning: Avoid Third-Party Scams\nWhen searching for Georgia tag renewals online, you may run into third-party \"concierge\" websites (such as *GeorgiaCarReg* or similar privately-run sites). \n* These sites are **not** official government portals. \n* They charge heavy, unnecessary service fees (often $40 or more) simply to submit your information to the real state portal on your behalf. \n* **Always verify** that you are on a website ending in **`.gov`** (such as `ga.gov` or `georgia.gov`) before entering your personal, vehicle, or credit card information.",
